### ⚡ In 30 seconds
- else pairs with the nearest if.
- Use braces to avoid dangling else.
- max = a > b ? a : b;

---

## Nested if-else
```c
if (a > b) {
    if (a > c) max = a; else max = c;
} else {
    if (b > c) max = b; else max = c;
}
```
## Dangling else
**An `else` pairs with the nearest unmatched `if`.**
```c
if (a > 0)
    if (b > 0) printf("both");
else printf("a not positive?");   // actually belongs to if (b > 0)!
```
Use braces to force the pairing you mean.

## Conditional (ternary) operator
`result = condition ? expr1 : expr2;`
- `max = (a > b) ? a : b;`
- Largest of three: `max = a > b ? (a > c ? a : c) : (b > c ? b : c);`
- Right-to-left associative; it's an expression, so it can sit inside `printf`.
